Immuch360 Desktop: brush_app as a trainer without window, network, rerun or LPIPS weights

Brush v0.3.0 (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/ArthurBrussee/brush, commit 3edecbb2fe79d3e2c87eeab85b15e0b1dd10d486),
modified by the Immuch360 project on 1 November 2026. Each file this patch changes carries a line saying so, as the
Apache License 2.0 asks (section 4 b). Applied by .github/desktop/ai/brush_build.py sources before
cargo build --locked: no dependency is added or removed, so Cargo.lock of the tag stays as it is.

Four parts of Brush become cargo features, all off unless asked for:
  - brush-app "viewer" (on by default, as upstream): the window (egui, eframe, winit, brush-ui). Built without it,
    brush_app only trains from a path given on the command line and refuses --with-viewer.
  - brush-train "lpips": the LPIPS loss and its VGG weights (crates/lpips/burn_mapped.bin, 29,433,386 bytes, whose
    provenance is not written in the repository). Without it, a --lpips-loss-weight above 0 is refused at the start
    (its default is 0, which Immuch360 never changes).
  - brush-process "rerun": logging to a rerun.io viewer (a gRPC client and server). Without it, --rerun-enabled only
    logs a warning.
  - brush-vfs "pick" and "url": the file dialogs (rfd) and the sources given by a URL (reqwest). Without them, such a
    source is refused with a message.
brush-ui asks for "pick", "url" and "rerun", so a build with the viewer keeps what upstream has, the LPIPS loss apart.

